# The whole production folder stays out of git (owner, 24 Sep 2026).
# It is 4.9 GB of video, audio and frame sequences, and git keeps every binary
# blob forever - committing it would put ~141 MB into every clone permanently,
# including the coworker's, and removing it later would need a history rewrite
# on a shared branch. The deliverables live in the Drive folder, which is where
# they are actually delivered from. The specific rules above are kept because
# they record what each subfolder is.
/outputs/
